# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  logosservices.la — LogosServices, the service manager (Citrinitas layer 13).
#
#  WHAT. SVC_KIT(B)(X) returns la s. s(manager). manager(descs)(channel)(logdir)
#  runs the supervisor of the system's background services, each its own LA
#  program in its own process (OS_LAYERS_DESIGN.md, "logosservices.la"):
#
#    desc = la k. k(name)(path)(args)(deps)(restart)
#      name     1-64 characters of [A-Za-z0-9_.-]; its log is logdir/<name>.log
#      path     the executable (a bundle: VM + compiled stream, bundle.la)
#      args     its whole argv as one space-separated string, argv[0] first
#      deps     a Scott list of the names it needs started first (the
#               manager's own name, logosservices, is always satisfied)
#      restart  "always" | "on-failure" | "never"
#
#  The manager
#    1. checks the descriptors and orders them by dependency. A cycle, a
#       missing dependency, a duplicate or malformed name or an unknown policy
#       is a loud error (exit 1) before anything starts;
#    2. starts the services in that order: pipe + fork; the child resets its
#       signal mask, takes /dev/null as stdin and the pipe as stdout AND
#       stderr, closes every other fd, and execv's the program. A failed
#       execv writes its error into the log and exits 127 (logosinit.la's
#       guard against a child continuing as a second manager);
#    3. then loops, one pass per wake-up of ONE poll over the control socket,
#       a signalfd and every service's pipe (100 ms tick):
#         - output ready on a pipe is appended to that service's log;
#         - exits are reaped without blocking (see REAPING below);
#         - an exited service is restarted per its policy after a backoff
#           that doubles from 1 s (1, 2, 4, 8, 16 s). After 5 restarts in a
#           row it is given up and marked `failed`. A run that lasted 10 s
#           or more ends the row: the count starts again from 0;
#         - when poll says the control socket is ready (and only then), one
#           client is accepted and its one typed logosipc request served;
#         - SIGTERM or SIGINT (blocked, read off the signalfd) shuts down.
#
#  CONTROL. Requests are logosipc typed messages (TYPE <NUL> BODY) on the
#  channel `channel` (the AF_UNIX path /tmp/logosipc-<channel>); the reply's
#  type is `ok` or `err`, and the connection is closed after it.
#      status            one line per service, "name state pid restarts",
#                        the manager itself first as "logosservices running
#                        <its pid> 0". States: running, backoff (waiting to be
#                        restarted), stopped, exited (ended with status 0 and
#                        not restarted), failed. pid is 0 when none runs.
#      stop <name>       SIGTERM, wait up to 3 s, then SIGKILL; reaped before
#                        the reply. A stopped service is not restarted.
#      start <name>      start it now (cancelling any backoff); the restart
#                        count starts again from 0.
#      restart <name>    stop if running, then start.
#      shutdown          stop every service, last started first; reply; exit 0.
#  `restarts` in a status line counts the restarts in the current row.
#  SELF-APPLICATION. The manager is itself a service of the manager: it is
#  listed as `logosservices`, keeps its own log beside theirs
#  (logdir/logosservices.log, every event it acts on, stamped with monotonic
#  milliseconds), `stop logosservices` is shutdown, and `restart
#  logosservices` stops everything and re-executes its own program (argv[0]
#  when that is a path, else /proc/self/exe) — the same pid becomes a fresh
#  manager, which starts every service again.
#
#  WHY. The Codex's layer 13: "Background processes: time sync, DNS
#  resolution, power management …" and "LogosServices services itself (system
#  services are services managed by the service manager)". logosinit.la
#  supervises one shell; this supervises any number of LA programs, in order,
#  with logs, policies and a control channel.
#
#  USE. A manager program builds the two records and the descriptors and calls
#  the manager once (it never returns):
#      import("logosservices.la")
#      glyph MAIN = SVC_KIT(<B>)(<X>)(la manager.
#          manager(CONS(<time desc>)(CONS(<ledger desc>)(NIL)))("services")("logs"))
#  logostime.la and logosledger.la are the two system services;
#  gate_logosservices.sh runs a ten-service set and is the reference use.
#  Measured on the VM: an idle pass costs ~0.3 ms of CPU (one service); a
#  control request answers in ~3 ms (~16 ms with the client VM's own start);
#  stop is ~120 ms (the service's SIGTERM handling and the reap); start ~20 ms.
#
#  REAPING. This VM's reapnb returns a pid but throws the exit status away, and
#  waitpid blocks. So each pass reads /proc/<pid>/stat of every running service:
#  a process in state Z has exited, field 52 of that line is its raw wait status
#  (exit code << 8, or the signal), and waitpid on a zombie returns at once. The
#  state is found after the LAST ')' of the line, so a process that renames
#  itself cannot fake an exit. /proc must be mounted; the manager checks it at
#  startup. "failure" is any non-zero raw status (non-zero exit or a signal).
#
#  ARGV. This VM's execv(path)(args) puts `path` in argv[0] itself and makes
#  argv[1..] from `args`, so the manager passes `args` without its first word.
#
#  STYLE. Kit style (WM_DESIGN.md "How fast the VM is"): every builtin arrives in
#  the records B and X, SVC_KIT applies them once, and the running loop finds
#  every name in its environment. Its own messages are decoded with logosipc's
#  MSG_TYPE/MSG_BODY, which walk only the few-byte type tag.
#    B = la s. s(str_at)(ord)(str_to_int)(int_to_str)(concat)(str_eq)(str_len)
#                (add)(sub)(mul)(div)(mod)(lt)(int_eq)(bshl)
#    X = la s. s(fork)(execv)(dup2)(pipe)(open)(close)(read)(write)(poll)(kill)
#                (waitpid)(clock_gettime)(getpid)(sigprocmask)(signalfd)(socket)
#                (connect)(unlink)(read_file)(stat)(mkdir)(exit)(error)
#  VM only: fork, execv, pipe, poll, sockets and signals exist only there.
#
#  HONEST SCOPE. A service's own children are not tracked: no process groups or
#  cgroups (the VM has no setsid), so stop signals the service's pid only. There
#  is no readiness protocol — dependency order is start order. One control
#  request is served at a time, read with one recv (a request is a few bytes;
#  a client silent for 2 s is dropped). A second manager is refused a channel
#  that a live manager already serves.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

import("logosipc.la")

export SVC_KIT

glyph Z   = la f. (la x. f(la v. x(x)(v)))(la x. f(la v. x(x)(v)))
glyph LET = la v. la k. k(v)

# ── Scott lists ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SV_LISTS(B) -> la s. s(nil)(cons)(map)(filter)(find)(all)(len)(rev)
# map applies f in list order (call-by-value evaluates cons's head first).
glyph SV_LISTS = la B. B(la str_at. la ord. la str_to_int. la int_to_str. la concat. la str_eq.
    la str_len. la add. la sub. la mul. la div. la mod. la lt. la int_eq. la bshl.
  (la C0. la C1. la TRUE. la FALSE. la nil. la cons.
    LET(Z(la map. la f. la l. l(la _. nil)(la h. la t. cons(f(h))(map(f)(t)))))(la map.
    LET(Z(la filter. la p. la l.
        l(la _. nil)(la h. la t. p(h)(la _. cons(h)(filter(p)(t)))(la _. filter(p)(t))(C0))))(la filter.
    LET(Z(la find. la p. la l.
        l(la _. la none. la some. none(none))
         (la h. la t. p(h)(la _. la none. la some. some(h))(la _. find(p)(t))(C0))))(la find.
    LET(Z(la all. la p. la l.
        l(la _. TRUE)(la h. la t. p(h)(la _. all(p)(t))(la _. FALSE)(C0))))(la all.
    LET(Z(la len. la l. l(la _. C0)(la h. la t. add(C1)(len(t)))))(la len.
    LET(Z(la rev. la acc. la l. l(la _. acc)(la h. la t. rev(cons(h)(acc))(t))))(la revacc.
      la s. s(nil)(cons)(map)(filter)(find)(all)(len)(revacc(nil)))))))))
  (0)(1)(la t. la f. t)(la t. la f. f)(la n. la c. n(n))(la h. la t. la n. la c. c(h)(t)))

# ── Text ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SV_TEXT(B)(L) -> la s. s(slice)(words)(joinsp)(joinnl)(member)(digits)(okname)(nth)
#   slice(s)(lo)(hi)  bytes lo..hi-1, joined by halving (O(n log n))
#   words(s)          the space-separated words of s (empty words dropped)
#   joinsp / joinnl   join a list with " " / "\n"
#   member(x)(l)      is the string x in the list l
#   digits(s)         s is one or more decimal digits
#   okname(s)         1-64 characters of [A-Za-z0-9_.-], not "." or ".."
#   nth(k)(l)         option: the k-th element (from 0)
glyph SV_TEXT = la B. la L. B(la str_at. la ord. la str_to_int. la int_to_str. la concat. la str_eq.
    la str_len. la add. la sub. la mul. la div. la mod. la lt. la int_eq. la bshl.
  L(la nil. la cons. la map. la filter. la find. la all. la len. la rev.
  (la C0. la C1. la C2. la C45. la C46. la C48. la C57. la C64. la C65. la C90. la C95.
   la C97. la C122. la TRUE. la FALSE.
    LET(Z(la slice. la s. la lo. la hi.
        lt(lo)(hi)
          (la _. int_eq(sub(hi)(lo))(C1)
                   (la _. str_at(s)(lo))
                   (la _. (la mid. concat(slice(s)(lo)(mid))(slice(s)(mid)(hi)))(div(add(lo)(hi))(C2)))(C0))
          (la _. "")(C0)))(la slice.
    LET(Z(la go. la s. la n. la i. la start.
        int_eq(i)(n)
          (la _. lt(start)(i)(la _. cons(slice(s)(start)(i))(nil))(la _. nil)(C0))
          (la _. (la i1. str_eq(str_at(s)(i))(" ")
                    (la _. lt(start)(i)(la _. cons(slice(s)(start)(i))(go(s)(n)(i1)(i1)))
                                       (la _. go(s)(n)(i1)(i1))(C0))
                    (la _. go(s)(n)(i1)(start))(C0))
                 (add(i)(C1)))(C0)))(la wgo.
    LET(la s. wgo(s)(str_to_int(str_len(s)))(C0)(C0))(la words.
    LET(la sep. Z(la join. la l.
        l(la _. "")(la h. la t. t(la _. h)(la h2. la t2. concat(h)(concat(sep)(join(t)))))))(la joinby.
    LET(joinby(" "))(la joinsp.
    LET(joinby("\n"))(la joinnl.
    LET(la x. la l. find(la y. str_eq(y)(x))(l)(la _. FALSE)(la y. TRUE))(la member.
    # every(p)(s)(i)(n): p holds for the byte value of each of s[i..n-1]
    LET(Z(la every. la p. la s. la i. la n.
        int_eq(i)(n)(la _. TRUE)
          (la _. p(str_to_int(ord(str_at(s)(i))))(la _. every(p)(s)(add(i)(C1))(n))(la _. FALSE)(C0))(C0)))(la every.
    LET(la lo. la hi. la c. lt(c)(lo)(FALSE)(lt(hi)(c)(FALSE)(TRUE)))(la within.
    LET(la s. (la n. lt(C0)(n)(la _. every(within(C48)(C57))(s)(C0)(n))(la _. FALSE)(C0))
        (str_to_int(str_len(s))))(la digits.
    LET(la c. within(C48)(C57)(c)(TRUE)(within(C65)(C90)(c)(TRUE)(within(C97)(C122)(c)(TRUE)(
        int_eq(c)(C45)(TRUE)(int_eq(c)(C46)(TRUE)(int_eq(c)(C95)))))))(la namechar.
    LET(la s. (la n.
        lt(C0)(n)
          (la _. lt(C64)(n)(la _. FALSE)(la _.
                   str_eq(s)(".")(la _. FALSE)(la _.
                   str_eq(s)("..")(la _. FALSE)(la _. every(namechar)(s)(C0)(n))(C0))(C0))(C0))
          (la _. FALSE)(C0))
        (str_to_int(str_len(s))))(la okname.
    LET(Z(la nth. la k. la l.
        l(la _. la none. la some. none(none))
         (la h. la t. int_eq(k)(C0)(la _. la none. la some. some(h))(la _. nth(sub(k)(C1))(t))(C0))))(la nth.
      la s. s(slice)(words)(joinsp)(joinnl)(member)(digits)(okname)(nth)))))))))))))))
  (0)(1)(2)(45)(46)(48)(57)(64)(65)(90)(95)(97)(122)(la t. la f. t)(la t. la f. f)))

# ── The manager's static parts ────────────────────────────────────────────
# SV_CORE(B)(X)(L)(T)(ipc) -> la s. s(now)(mk)(dname)(rname)(rstate)(rpid)(rrfd)
#                                    (dead)(drain)(closeall)(child)(topo)(waitdead)(must)(listen)
#                                    (selfpath)
# A supervised service is rec = la k. k(desc)(state)(pid)(restarts)(rfd)(lfd)(due)(t0):
# rfd the read end of its output pipe ("" when closed), lfd its log fd, due the
# monotonic ms at which a backoff restart is due, t0 when it last started.
glyph SV_CORE = la B. la X. la L. la T. la ipc.
  B(la str_at. la ord. la str_to_int. la int_to_str. la concat. la str_eq.
    la str_len. la add. la sub. la mul. la div. la mod. la lt. la int_eq. la bshl.
  X(la fork. la execv. la dup2. la pipe. la open. la close. la read. la write. la poll.
    la kill. la waitpid. la clock_gettime. la getpid. la sigprocmask. la signalfd. la socket.
    la connect. la unlink. la read_file. la stat. la mkdir. la exit. la error.
  L(la nil. la cons. la map. la filter. la find. la all. la len. la rev.
  T(la slice. la words. la joinsp. la joinnl. la member. la digits. la okname. la nth.
  ipc(la CHANNEL. la ACCEPT. la SEND. la RECV. la MSG_TYPE. la MSG_BODY.
  (la C0. la C1. la C2. la C3. la C4. la C9. la C17. la C30. la C49. la C256. la C1000. la C1000000.
   la TRUE. la FALSE.
    LET("logosservices")(la MGR.
    LET(sub(C0)(C1))(la NEG1.
    # now(_): the monotonic clock in milliseconds
    LET(la _. (la w. w(la _. C0)(la s. la r. r(la _. mul(str_to_int(s))(C1000))
          (la ns. la r2. add(mul(str_to_int(s))(C1000))(div(str_to_int(ns))(C1000000)))))
        (words(clock_gettime("1"))))(la now.
    LET(la d. la st. la pid. la r. la rfd. la lfd. la due. la t0.
        la k. k(d)(st)(pid)(r)(rfd)(lfd)(due)(t0))(la mk.
    LET(la d. d(la name. la path. la args. la deps. la restart. name))(la dname.
    LET(la rec. rec(la d. la st. la pid. la r. la rfd. la lfd. la due. la t0. dname(d)))(la rname.
    LET(la rec. rec(la d. la st. la pid. la r. la rfd. la lfd. la due. la t0. st))(la rstate.
    LET(la rec. rec(la d. la st. la pid. la r. la rfd. la lfd. la due. la t0. pid))(la rpid.
    LET(la rec. rec(la d. la st. la pid. la r. la rfd. la lfd. la due. la t0. rfd))(la rrfd.
    # lastparen(s)(i): the index of the last ")" at or before i, or -1
    LET(Z(la lp. la s. la i.
        lt(i)(C0)(la _. NEG1)
          (la _. str_eq(str_at(s)(i))(")")(la _. i)(la _. lp(s)(sub(i)(C1)))(C0))(C0)))(la lastparen.
    LET(Z(la fs. la s. la n. la i.
        int_eq(i)(n)(la _. n)
          (la _. str_eq(str_at(s)(i))("/")(la _. i)(la _. fs(s)(n)(add(i)(C1)))(C0))(C0)))(la firstslash.
    # dead(pid): none while the process runs; some(raw wait status) once it is a
    # zombie (-1 if the status field cannot be read, which counts as a failure).
    # The line is "<pid> (<name>) <state> ..."; the state is the first field
    # after the LAST ')', and the kernel keeps a name to 15 bytes, so that ')'
    # is at most at index len(pid)+17: the scan back starts there, not at the
    # end of the ~300-byte line (this check runs for every service every pass).
    LET(la pid. (la st. (la n. (la p.
          lt(p)(C0)(la _. la none. la some. none(none))(la _.
          lt(add(p)(C2))(n)
            (la _. str_eq(str_at(st)(add(p)(C2)))("Z")
              (la _. (la end.
                  nth(C49)(words(slice(st)(add(p)(C2))(end)))
                    (la _. la none. la some. some(NEG1))
                    (la f. la none. la some. some(digits(f)(la _. str_to_int(f))(la _. NEG1)(C0))))
                (str_eq(str_at(st)(sub(n)(C1)))("\n")(la _. sub(n)(C1))(la _. n)(C0)))
              (la _. la none. la some. none(none))(C0))
            (la _. la none. la some. none(none))(C0))(C0))
        (lt(n)(C4)(la _. NEG1)
           (la _. (la top. lastparen(st)(lt(top)(n)(la _. top)(la _. sub(n)(C1))(C0)))
                  (add(str_to_int(str_len(pid)))(C17)))(C0)))
      (str_to_int(str_len(st))))
      (read_file(concat("/proc/")(concat(pid)("/stat")))))(la dead.
    # drain(rfd)(lfd): copy what is left in a dead service's pipe into its log,
    # never blocking (poll with timeout 0 before each read), then close it
    LET(Z(la drain. la rfd. la lfd.
        str_eq(rfd)("")(la _. C0)(la _.
          str_eq(poll(rfd)("0"))("")
            (la _. close(rfd))
            (la _. (la data. str_eq(data)("")
                      (la _. close(rfd))
                      (la _. (la _. drain(rfd)(lfd))(write(lfd)(data)))(C0))
                   (read(rfd)("65536")))(C0))(C0)))(la drain.
    LET(Z(la ca. la i. lt(i)(C256)(la _. (la _. ca(add(i)(C1)))(close(int_to_str(i))))(la _. C0)(C0)))(la closeall.
    # this VM's execv puts path in argv[0] itself: pass args without its first word
    LET(la args. words(args)(la _. "")(la h. la t. joinsp(t)))(la argtail.
    # child(wfd)(path)(args): the forked side of a start; never returns
    LET(la wfd. la path. la args.
        (la _.
          (la _.
            (la _.
              (la _.
                (la _.
                  (la e. (la _. exit("127"))
                         (write("2")(concat("logosservices: execv ")(concat(path)(concat(" failed: ")(concat(e)("\n")))))))
                  (execv(path)(argtail(args))))
                (closeall(C3)))
              (dup2(wfd)("2")))
            (dup2(wfd)("1")))
          ((la nf. dup2(nf)("0"))(open("/dev/null")("0"))))
        (sigprocmask("2")("0")))(la child.
    # kahn(remaining)(started names)(order so far, reversed)
    LET(Z(la kahn. la rem. la done. la out.
        rem(la _. rev(out))
           (la h. la t.
              find(la d. d(la name. la path. la args. la deps. la restart. all(la x. member(x)(done))(deps)))(rem)
                (la _. error(concat("logosservices: dependency cycle among: ")(joinsp(map(dname)(rem)))))
                (la d. (la n. kahn(filter(la e. str_eq(dname(e))(n)(la _. FALSE)(la _. TRUE)(C0))(rem))
                                  (cons(n)(done))(cons(d)(out)))
                       (dname(d))))))(la kahn.
    # topo(descs): check every descriptor, then the start order. The manager
    # counts as started: a service may depend on logosservices itself.
    LET(la descs. (la names.
        (la _. kahn(descs)(cons(MGR)(nil))(nil))
        (map(la d. d(la name. la path. la args. la deps. la restart.
            (la _. (la _. (la _.
                map(la x. member(x)(cons(MGR)(names))(la _. C0)
                      (la _. error(concat("logosservices: ")(concat(name)(concat(": missing dependency ")(x)))))(C0))(deps))
              (str_eq(restart)("always")(la _. C0)(la _. str_eq(restart)("on-failure")(la _. C0)(la _.
               str_eq(restart)("never")(la _. C0)(la _.
                 error(concat("logosservices: ")(concat(name)(concat(": unknown restart policy ")(restart)))))(C0))(C0))(C0)))
              (lt(C1)(len(filter(la m. str_eq(m)(name))(names)))
                 (la _. error(concat("logosservices: duplicate service ")(name)))(la _. C0)(C0)))
            (okname(name)
               (la _. str_eq(name)(MGR)
                        (la _. error(concat("logosservices: the name ")(concat(MGR)(" is the manager's own"))))
                        (la _. C0)(C0))
               (la _. error(concat("logosservices: bad service name: ")(name)))(C0))))(descs)))
      (map(dname)(descs)))(la topo.
    # waitdead(pid)(i): reap pid after a SIGTERM, waiting up to 30 x 100 ms,
    # then SIGKILL; returns the raw status
    LET(Z(la waitdead. la pid. la i.
        dead(pid)
          (la _. lt(i)(C30)
                   (la _. (la _. waitdead(pid)(add(i)(C1)))(poll("")("100")))
                   (la _. (la _. (la _. C9)(waitpid(pid)))(kill(pid)("9")))(C0))
          (la raw. (la _. raw)(waitpid(pid)))))(la waitdead.
    # selfpath(_): what `restart logosservices` re-executes: argv[0] when it is
    # a path that exists (so the new image keeps its name in ps), else
    # /proc/self/exe
    LET(Z(la go. la s. la n. la i.
        int_eq(i)(n)(la _. n)
          (la _. int_eq(str_to_int(ord(str_at(s)(i))))(C0)(la _. i)(la _. go(s)(n)(add(i)(C1)))(C0))(C0)))(la firstnul.
    LET(la _. (la cl. (la a0.
          (la n0. (la hasslash.
              hasslash(la _. str_eq(str_at(stat(a0))(C0))("-")(la _. "/proc/self/exe")(la _. a0)(C0))
                      (la _. "/proc/self/exe")(C0))
            (lt(C0)(n0)(la _. lt(firstslash(a0)(n0)(C0))(n0))(la _. FALSE)(C0)))
          (str_to_int(str_len(a0))))
        (slice(cl)(C0)(firstnul(cl)(str_to_int(str_len(cl)))(C0))))
      (read_file("/proc/self/cmdline")))(la selfpath.
    LET(la fd. la what. digits(fd)(la _. fd)
        (la _. error(concat("logosservices: cannot open ")(concat(what)(concat(" (")(concat(fd)(")"))))))(C0))(la must.
    # listen(channel)(sock): refuse a channel a live server answers on, then
    # CHANNEL it and check the socket exists
    LET(la channel. la sock. (la probe. (la r. (la _.
          str_eq(r)("0")
            (la _. error(concat("logosservices: the channel ")(concat(channel)(" is already served"))))
            (la _. (la lfd. str_eq(str_at(stat(sock))(C0))("-")
                      (la _. error(concat("logosservices: cannot listen on the channel ")(channel)))
                      (la _. lfd)(C0))
                   (CHANNEL(channel)))(C0))
          (close(probe)))(connect(probe)(sock)))(socket("!")))(la listen.
      la s. s(now)(mk)(dname)(rname)(rstate)(rpid)(rrfd)(dead)(drain)(closeall)(child)(topo)(waitdead)(must)(listen)
             (selfpath)
    ))))))))))))))))))))))))
  (0)(1)(2)(3)(4)(9)(17)(30)(49)(256)(1000)(1000000)(la t. la f. t)(la t. la f. f))))))

# ── The running manager ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SV_RUN(B)(X)(L)(T)(ipc)(core) -> la order. la sock. la sfd. la mfd. la lfd. la channel. la logdir.
# starts the services of `order` and runs the supervision loop; never returns.
glyph SV_RUN = la B. la X. la L. la T. la ipc. la core.
  B(la str_at. la ord. la str_to_int. la int_to_str. la concat. la str_eq.
